WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.664
Likert-style responses illustrate ordinal data well
A five is

00:00:05.691 --> 00:00:09.901
higher than a four but the psychological distance
from one to two may not equal

00:00:09.914 --> 00:00:15.436
the distance from four to five Means are commonly
reported in practice

00:00:15.647 --> 00:00:21.564
particularly for composite scales But for a single
coarse item medians

00:00:21.682 --> 00:00:28.064
distributions and rank-based summaries may better
respect the measurement assumptions The

00:00:28.077 --> 00:00:32.656
important point is to recognize the assumption
rather than use the mean automatically
